From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NP <50584693+NatePu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:06:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] T1.2: flow table core, ddb commands, boot self-test

- net/if_flow.c: SipHash-2-4 buckets; flow_lookup() for SMR readers;
  flow_table_add() under flow_mtx (live same-key same-gen = duplicate,
  dead or stale same-key entry unlinked first, net.flow.max = full);
  flow_unlink() marks DEAD and frees via smr_call(); flow_alloc().
- Mode transition step 5: flush bucket by bucket, then smr_barrier().
- flow:0:stats gains "yield" with flow_count_yield() (ERRATA E83).
- ddb: show flows [/count], show flow <addr> (db_command.c,
  db_interface.h).
- DIAGNOSTIC boot self-test: insert, lookup, absent key, duplicate,
  stale replacement, unlink, full, 64 keys; one result line, no panic.
  FLOW_SELFTEST builds it alone for the host-side harness.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
